                                                                <p dir=3D"l=
tr" style=3D"text-align: justify;"><span>In this article, we=E2=80=99ll wal=
k through the step-by-step process of creating a Real-Time Polling App usin=
g NodeJS, ExpressJS, and socket.io. This project will showcase how to set u=
p a web application where users can perform real-time polling.</span></p><p=
 dir=3D"ltr"><b><strong>Preview of final output: </strong></b><span>Let us =
have a look at how the final application will look like:</span></p><p dir=
=3D"ltr"><img alt=3D"polling" height=3D"435" src=3D"https://media.geeksforg=
eeks.org/wp-content/uploads/20240301014551/polling.jpg" width=3D"768"></p><=
h2><b><strong>Prerequisites:</strong></b></h2><ul><li value=3D"1"><a href=
=3D"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/node-js-npm-node-package-manager/" rel=3D=
"noopener" target=3D"_blank"><span>NPM &amp; NodeJS</span></a></li><li valu=
e=3D"2"><a href=3D"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/react-tutorial/" rel=3D"no=
opener" target=3D"_blank"><span>ReactJS</span></a></li><li value=3D"3"><a h=
ref=3D"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/express-js/" rel=3D"noopener" target=
=3D"_blank"><span>ExpressJS</span></a></li><li value=3D"4"><a href=3D"https=
://www.geeksforgeeks.org/how-to-manage-users-in-socket-io-in-node-js/" rel=
=3D"noopener" target=3D"_blank"><span>Socket.io</span></a></li></ul><h2><sp=
an>Approach to create a Real-time Polling Application:</span></h2><ul><li v=
alue=3D"1"><span>The</span><b><strong> </strong></b><b><code><strong>BarCha=
rt</strong></code></b><b><strong> component</strong></b><span> is a visual =
representation of poll data for different backend frameworks.</span></li><l=
i value=3D"2"><span>It receives real-time updates via a WebSocket connectio=
n using the </span><b><code><strong>socket.io-client</strong></code></b><sp=
an> library.</span></li><li value=3D"3"><span>The component displays a bar =
chart with vote counts for each framework and allows users to cast votes by=
 clicking on corresponding buttons.</span></li><li value=3D"4"><span>Establ=
ishes a WebSocket connection using </span><b><code><strong>io('http://local=
host:5000')</strong></code></b><span> via </span><a href=3D"https://www.gee=
ksforgeeks.org/react-js-usememo-hook/" rel=3D"noopener" target=3D"_blank"><=
code><span>useMemo</span></code></a><span>.</span></li><li value=3D"5"><spa=
n>Uses </span><a href=3D"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/reactjs-useeffect-ho=
ok/" rel=3D"noopener" target=3D"_blank"><code><span>useEffect</span></code>=
</a><span> to handle connection events and attempts to reconnect in case of=
 errors.</span></li><li value=3D"6"><span>Renders the </span><code><span>Ba=
rChart</span></code><span> component, passing the socket connection as a pr=
op.</span></li><li value=3D"7"><span>Creates an Express server and a Socket=
.io server.</span></li><li value=3D"8"><span>Defines an initial set of back=
end frameworks with vote counts.</span></li><li value=3D"9"><span>Handles <=
/span><a href=3D"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/what-is-web-socket-and-how-i=
t-is-different-from-the-http/" rel=3D"noopener" target=3D"_blank"><span>Web=
Socket</span></a><span> connections and updates in real-time.</span></li><l=
i value=3D"10"><span>Logs user connections, emits initial data, and updates=
 data on vote events</span></li></ul><h2><span>Steps to Create the Backend =
Server:</span></h2><p dir=3D"ltr"><b><strong>Step 1:</strong></b><span> Cre=
ate a directory for project</span></p><pre><span>mkdir server</span><br><sp=
an>cd server</span></pre><p dir=3D"ltr"><b><strong>Step 2</strong></b><span=
>: Initialized the Express app and installing the required packages</span><=
/p><div id=3D"GFG_AD_Desktop_InContent_ATF_728x280" style=3D"text-align: ce=
nter; margin: 10px 0px;"></div><pre><span>npm init -y</span></pre><p dir=3D=
"ltr"><b><strong>Step 3: </strong></b><span>Install the required dependency=
 in your server using the following command.</span></p><pre><span>npm i exp=
ress nodemon socket.io </span></pre><h3><span>Project Structure:</span></h3=
><p dir=3D"ltr"><img alt=3D"Screenshot-2024-03-01-015849" height=3D"276" lo=
